      "side": 1,
      "message": "We need the PHY switching to be part of what\u0027s in board/$BOARD/ too. We may not *want* to switch PHYs until we\u0027re told to, or until the AP USB has suspended, or something like that. Same for turning it off - the x20 design docs suggested leaving CCD enabled after detaching until the AP powers off.\n\nSo the interrupt handler would just be:\n\n  if (debug_cable_is_detected()) {\n    GWRITE(RDD, PROG_DEBUG_STATE_MAP, ~ccd_detect);\n    rdd_attached();\n  } else {\n    GWRITE(RDD, PROG_DEBUG_STATE_MAP, ccd_detect);\n    rdd_detached();\n  }\n\nand you could declare rdd_attached() and rdd_detached() in chip/g/rdd.h",
